          "settings": {
            "heading": "How do I know what driver to buy when using LED strip?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Selecting the right driver (PSU) is often the trickiest part of an LED strip set-up. Work through it like this:</p><ol><li>Check the watts per metre (wpm) of your strip — this is on the technical spec supplied with it.</li><li>Work out how many metres of strip you're using.</li><li>Multiply the two together. E.g. 10wpm strip over a 5m run = 5m × 10w = 50w.</li><li>Add headroom — a good rule of thumb is 20%. So 50w × 1.2 = 60w. Look for a driver rated 60w or higher.</li><li>Decide whether you need a standard (non-dimmable) or dimmable driver, based on how the set-up will be controlled — a conventional switch, or 0–10V / mains / DALI / smart home dimming.</li></ol><p>If you're unsure, call us and we'll talk you through it.</p>"
          }
        }
